cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below, and cite the data sources (Cook et al. 2019, Witvliet et al. 2021, White et al. 1986, OpenWorm c302)."
title: "XRPLife: a complete connectome as ledger objects (C. elegans on the XRP Ledger, with a four-animal life cycle)"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LeDenti/xrplife"
authors:
  - family-names: Cugny
    given-names: Julien
keywords:
  - connectome
  - C. elegans
  - XRP Ledger
  - XRPL
  - blockchain
  - OpenWorm
  - developmental connectome
abstract: >-
  The complete wired connectome of C. elegans (302 neurons, Cook et al. 2019)
  materialised on the XRP Ledger testnet: every neuron is an account issuing its
  own currency, every directed synaptic pair a trust line held by the postsynaptic
  neuron (limit = synaptic weight), the dataset hash anchored in a memo, a nerve
  impulse a chain of payments. A complete life cycle of four animals (eggs, growth
  through Witvliet 2021 and Cook 2019 connectomes, mating by Check, egg laying,
  death by account deletion) was run in four hours of ledger time, with XRP reserve
  as food. Preprint in paper/xrplife.pdf.
